# Canvas removal request, rename and destroy signals. obs_canvas_remove only flags the canvas and
# announces it; it does not drop any reference. Removing twice, or removing the main canvas, is a
# no-op. Private canvases do not emit the core-level create/remove/rename/destroy signals, but still
# emit the per-canvas ones.
startup en-US -
sig_obs canvas_create canvas_remove canvas_destroy canvas_rename canvas_video_reset
canvas_create a Alpha
sig_canvas a destroy remove rename video_reset
canvas_name a Beta
canvas_name a Beta
canvas_name a -
canvas_name a ""
canvas_remove a
canvas_remove a
canvas_info a
canvas_save a
enum canvases
get canvas_by_name Beta
canvas_create_private p Priv
sig_canvas p destroy remove rename
canvas_name p Priv2
canvas_remove p
canvas_release p
canvas_release a
shutdown
